# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers/CI — a CRLF checkout breaks them
# ("\r: command not found"). Force LF regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
# Rust sources: LF in every checkout. Several tests scan them for wiring, and a CRLF
# checkout (core.autocrlf=true) must not change what they see. The scans also fold
# line endings, so a working copy checked out before this rule still passes.
*.rs text eol=lf
